msm_drm (display techpack, Qualcomm r7 + Samsung panel framework): 6.18 DRM core

Every change follows a 6.12 -> 6.18 change of the DRM/IOMMU/MM core API; the Samsung
panel code (msm/samsung, S6E3FC3_AMS646YD01) needed none. Nothing in the UBWC / SSPP /
panel command paths is touched.

- drm_bridge_funcs.attach(bridge, encoder, flags): dsi, dp, dp_mst bridges take
  the encoder argument (unused; they get it from bridge->encoder as before).
- drm_connector_helper_funcs.mode_valid takes a const mode: sde_connector's hook is
  const and casts for the c_conn->ops.mode_valid chain (the mode is a probed_modes entry,
  not a const object; dsi/dp/Samsung mode_valid callees keep their prototypes).
- drm_driver.date is gone.
- device_match_t takes const void * (compare_name_mdp, MDP5-only path).
- iommu_present() is gone: msm_iommu_present() (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_IOMMU_API)); on
  this platform the SMMU is a load dependency and the SDE context banks are components of
  the display device, so the old call was always true when the driver bound.
- mipi_dsi_dcs_set_tear_off() is gone: its body, mipi_dsi_dcs_write(dsi,
  MIPI_DCS_SET_TEAR_OFF, NULL, 0) (poms TE work).
- linux/pfn_t.h is gone: vmf_insert_mixed() takes the pfn (6.12 passed
  PFN_DEV without PFN_MAP, i.e. not devmap: same special PTE either way on arm64).
- drm_get_format_info(dev, format, modifier); mode_config_funcs.fb_create receives
  the format info from the core; drm_helper_mode_fill_fb_struct() takes it too.
- drm_device.struct_mutex is gone: the driver used it as a device-wide lock around
  GEM frees and MADVISE; one msm_drm device, so one driver mutex (msm_drm_struct_mutex).
- FB_EVENT_BLANK left <linux/fb.h>: the Samsung suspend/resume notifier chain
  (msm_drm_register_notifier_client, exported) still sends it with the old value 0x09.
- DRM bridges are refcounted: drm_bridge_attach() takes a reference and
  drm_bridge_chain_get_first_bridge() returns one. msm_drm kzallocs/kfrees its bridges
  (dsi, dp, dp_mst), so their refcount was 0 and the first attach would WARN ("refcount_t:
  addition on 0; use-after-free") and saturate it. Now kref_init() before attach (msm_drm
  keeps owning the memory; the core never reaches 0) and msm_drm_first_bridge() drops the
  getter's reference at once (9 call sites), as 6.12 took none.
- drm_dp_dpcd_read_link_status() returns 0 on success (was the byte count 6): the DP
  link-status checks test for < 0, otherwise every read would be reported as a failure and
  dp_ctrl's ACT wait loop would bail out (DP only; the A52s has no DP output).

